#### Article 15

1. Prevention of acts of violence against children as referred to in Article 14 letter a shall be implemented by:  
a. establishing a network in efforts to prevent violence against children;  
b. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns with the community, private sector and non-governmental organizations; and  
c. conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to the protection of child victims of violence.  
2. Prevention of violence against children as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out in an integrated manner and coordinated by the Regional Apparatus having the main duties and functions in the field of women's empowerment and child protection.

#### Article 16

1. Prevention of acts of violence against children in addition to being implemented by the Regional Apparatus as referred to in Article 14 paragraph (2), also involves the parties:  
a. parents, family and / or closest relatives;  
b. community;  
c. vertical agencies;  
d. law enforcement apparatus;  
e. educational institutions;  
f. health institutions;  
g. religious institutions/organizations;h. social community institutions;
1. child social welfare institutions;  
J. business sector; and
k. other institutions engaged in the field of child protection care.  
2. Provisions regarding the involvement of parties as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be regulated in a Regent Regulation.

### Paragraph 3

Handling of Child Victims of Acts of Violence

#### Article 17

Handling of child victims of acts of violence as referred to in Article 14 letter b shall be implemented in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

### Paragraph 4

Rehabilitation of Child Victims of Acts of Violence

#### Article 18

Rehabilitation services as referred to in Article 14 letter c shall be carried out in the form of:  
a. legal aid services;  
b. health rehabilitation services;  
c. social rehabilitation services;  
d. repatriation and social reintegration services; and/ or  
e. restitution services for child victims of violence.  
2. In rehabilitation services as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government may cooperate with:  
a. vertical agencies;  
b. provincial government;  
c. other regency/city governments;  
d. village/sub-district government;  
e. non-governmental organizations;  
f. private parties;  
g. community; and/or  
h. family.

## Part Two

Special Protection of Children Article 19 (1) Special protection of children shall be provided to:  
a. children in emergency situations;  
b. children in conflict with the law;  
c. children from minority and isolated groups;  
d. children who are exploited economically and/ or sexually;  
e. children who are victims of narcotics, alcohol, psychotropic, and other addictive substance abuse;  
f. children who are victims of pornography;  
g. children with HIV/ AIDS;  
h. child victims of kidnapping, sale, and /or trafficking;  
1. child victims of physical and / or psychological Violence;  
J. child victims of sexual crimes;  
k. child victims of terrorism networks;  
1. children with disabilities:m. child victims of maltreatment and neglect;  
n. children with deviant social behavior; and  
o. children who are victims of stigmatization from labeling related to their parents' condition.  
2. The Regional Government in implementing the handling of special protection of children as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

# CHAPTER V

### INTEGRATED SERVICE CENTER FOR WOMEN'S EMPOWERMENT AND CHILDREN

#### Article 20

1. In the context of services for victims of acts of violence, the Regional Government shall establish P2TP2A.  
2. P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be stipulated by Regent Decree.

#### Article 21

1. P2TP2A as referred to in Article 20 shall have the duties to:  
a. provide services;  
b. provide protection to victims of acts of violence, reporters and witnesses; and  
c. conduct empowerment of victims of acts of violence.  
2. Services as referred to in paragraph (1) letter a shall include:  
a. receiving complaints/reports of Violence against women and/ or children, consultation, and counseling;  
b. receiving and sending case referrals from other Regency/City Regional Governments or institutions established by other Regency/City Regional Governments;  
c. providing legal assistance;  
d. health;  
e. social rehabilitation;  
f. legal aid services; and  
g. repatriation and social reintegration.

# CHAPTER VI

COOPERATION, OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES

## Part One

Cooperation

#### Article 22

In handling child victims of acts of violence as referred to in Article 18, the Regional Government may cooperate with:  
a. vertical agencies;  
b. provincial government;  
c. other regency /city governments;  
d. village /sub-district government;  
e. non-governmental organizations;  
f. private parties;  
g. community; and/orh. family.

#### Article 23

1. In certain cases the Regional Government may cooperate with;  
a. other Regional Governments;  
b. police;  
c. advocates;  
d. health workers;  
e. psychologists:f. social workers;  
g. volunteer companions;  
h. spiritual counselors;  
i. other law enforcers, to assist Victims in the court proceedings;  
J. National Commission on Violence Against Women;  
k. Indonesian Child Protection Commission or Child Protection Institution; and/or  
l. certain parties desired for the benefit of the victim.  
2. Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) may be in the form of:  
a. exchange of data and information;  
b. socialization;  
c. provision of legal aid:d. health services;  
e. psychological psychiatric services;  
f. victim assistance;  
g. counseling;  
h. social rehabilitation;  
i. spiritual guidance; and/or  
j. repatriation and social reintegration.

## Part Two

Obligations and Responsibilities

#### Article 24

1. Obligations and responsibilities in providing protection to (1) women and children from acts of violence shall be the joint responsibility of the Regional Government and the Community.  
2. Obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in paragraph (1). shall include:  
a. establishing, implementing policies, programs, and conducting cooperation activities in the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence;  
b. facilitating the establishment of institutional protection of women and children from acts of violence and providing support for facilities and infrastructure;  
c. allocating budget for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence according to the financial capacity of the Region;  
d. fostering and supervising the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence;  
e. providing protection services for women and child victims of acts of violence;  
f. encouraging and increasing community participation; and  
g. appointing parents and/ or substitute family caregivers as a protection measure for children who are victims of acts of violence.

# CHAPTER VII

### COMMUNITY AND BUSINESS SECTOR PARTICIPATION

#### Article 25

1. Every person may participate in providing protection to women and children from acts of violence.  
2. Participation as referred to in paragraph (1) may be carried out by:  
a. preventing and stopping the occurrence of acts of violence;  
b. providing protection to victims;  
c. providing first aid to victims of acts of violence;  
d. reporting acts of violence against women and /or children;  
e. independently socializing the rights of women and children;  
f. strengthening social community institutions in handling acts of violence against women and children; and/ or  
g. disseminating information about laws and regulations related to acts of violence against women and children.
